{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs | rg '/adrs?/'; sed -n '145,195p' docs/planning/decisions.md; sed -n '2390,2515p' docs/planning/decisions.md; cat docs/planning/chunks/C43.md docs/planning/reviews/C29/attempt-07/verdict-returned.json docs/planning/reviews/C28/attempt-09/receipt.json\"","aggregated_output":"docs/adr/0002-academy-shared-presentation.md\ndocs/adr/0001-native-operation-authority.md\ndocs/adr/0004-managed-workbench-admission.md\ndocs/adr/0003-native-harness-and-scoped-identity.md\nRead-only preflight found the new checkout already initialized on `main`, with\nthe exact origin and no worktree files. The remote advertised no branches.\nPlanning records were moved here from the framework checkout. This does not\nauthorize application implementation before the agreed planning/architecture gates.\n\n## D013 — Scan-key-first onboarding\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q13.\n\nThe first scan supports an explicit scanning API key without requiring management\nOAuth credentials. Support scan-only tenants. Management credentials are separate\nand added for administration workflows; a management registration does not\nimplicitly supply scan authentication. Additional scan credential modes must be\nspecified and tested when needed, not inferred from an SDK constructor.\n\n## D014 — Rust application authority\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q14.\n\nRust owns tenant context, credential access, request lifecycles, and permission\nto apply configuration changes. React presents drafts, reviews, and results.\nConfiguration review binds the tenant, credentials, resource, and draft; changed\ncontext invalidates it. Harness proposals enter the same operator review flow\nand cannot authorize Apply. Initially preserve the existing Harness project/tool\nrestrictions; expansion would require a separate explicit design decision.\n\n## D015 — Import work, reestablish authentication\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q15.\n\nImport selected user-authored work and settings, including saved cases, reports,\nAcademy drafts, API Client projects, and historical conversations. Require fresh\ncredential setup and sign-in. Regenerate disposable caches/downloads. Imported\nconversations are inspectable history until resumption compatibility is validated;\nold pending approvals and authentication sessions never transfer.\n\nReading protected source work for an explicitly selected import is distinct from\ntransferring its old authentication credentials. Define restartable import\nreceipts, version/account checks, rollback, and source-preservation tests.\n\n## D016 — Explicit offline behavior\n\nAccepted in interview round 4, Q16.\n\nOffline mode supports local drafts, saved work, history, and valid downloaded\nAcademy content. Online operations require explicit retry after reconnection.\nDo not silently replay configuration changes, scans, grading submissions, or\nother remote actions. Preserve unknown/uncertain outcomes rather than asserting\nthat cancellation or disconnection undid remote work.\n\n## D017 — Operational usage/cost administration\n\n## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-26 (\"I accept it as written\"), with authority to implement P09 end to end autonomously and to proceed with C28 while C26 remains in progress; every chunk is reviewed until it scores 9 in every dimension.\n\nThe owner explored fifteen interactive shell concepts on a Claude Design canvas\n(https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL), selected \"Refined\nNative\", and iterated its prototype (R2App, R2Onboard, R2Harness ×3,\nR2Rationale) through sixteen independent Codex usability reviews (scores 6, 7,\n7, then 8 on rounds 4–16). The prototype is frozen at canvas version 134 and\ncopied verbatim into `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` with a SHA-256\nmanifest; the canvas page is not changed again. Prototype data is invented and\nis never shipped.\n\nDecisions (grilling session, 55 questions, all recommendations accepted):\n\n1. Extraction is spec, then TypeScript presentation, then Rust contract, as\n   phase P09 chunks C27–C34 (see the chunk index). The first implementation\n   slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and add-tenant sheet.\n2. The prototype's state model is normative for twelve named invariants\n   (`docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md`) and illustrative for code shape.\n   Every prototype state field is assigned Rust-owned/observed or UI-transient\n   (`state-ownership.md`); nothing goes to browser storage.\n3. D014 holds: secrets enter only through the host secret sheet and vault;\n   an issued API key is disclosed only through the existing `RevealSecret`\n   host path, held for the active context and never persisted; key rotation\n   is the admitted sequence additional key (`Version`) → local deployment\n   acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback (no invented grace\n   period or revocation); typed-name confirmation is validated in the core;\n   tenant switch is refused by the core while a Harness decision is pending;\n   write-capable tool calls use the native confirmation sheet.\n3a. Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or\n   changed (Runtime Security, Gateway, Red Team and Model/skill reads).\n   Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as \"Not\n   available in this release\" with a dependency gate; no inventory,\n   verification result or mutation is invented for them.\n4. Tokens live in a local `--v2-*` file; Academy variables stay for the\n   embedded learner view. One Rust navigation inventory feeds the native menu,\n   sidebar and palette; ⌘1–⌘9 are menu-defined. Feature ids gain `home` and\n   `inbox`.\n5. The new shell ships behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag and the legacy\n   shell, flag and legacy acceptance scripts are removed in C34. The Academy\n   learner view is embedded unchanged.\n6. The wizard realises D013 (scan key first and only required credential);\n   v1 import is offered on the tenant step.\n7. Verification: Vitest fixtures named after every prototype wrapper board,\n   Rust tests per invariant, native acceptance extended with focus ring, live\n   regions, topmost modal and Reduce Motion persistence, screenshot evidence\n   at 100%/200% in both themes per chunk. Live calls only in C29 (verify,\n   Vulture, reads) and C31 (review apply, Redtail, prefixed) inside the scope\n   designated 2026-10-25. C27 is reviewed at 9/10 in every dimension and the\n   controller enforces it: a `docs_only` chunk has no native preparation or\n   acceptance and refuses owner acceptance at completion and at recognition;\n   C28–C34 follow D034.\n8. Minimum window 1180×720 with the rail collapsing below 1280 wide; toasts\n   persist under Reduce Motion; \"Show the calls\" panel shows diagnostics-\n   redacted wire data; English only in P09; chunks commit on main except C34.\n9. C27 proceeds in parallel with C26 (docs and controller registration only);\n   C28 waits for C26.\n\n\n## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-29 after a grilling session (23 questions, all\naccepted; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md`). C32 had taken twenty review rounds\nwhile the built v2 screens never matched the design: chunks had wrapped the\nlegacy feature components in v2 frames instead of porting the prototype.\n\n- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the\n  canvas is not consulted (it is unreachable from the implementing account).\n- A screen is done when it matches its board side by side at 1440×900 in both\n  themes with real core data, judged by the owner from composites kept under\n  the chunk's evidence; parity is structural (regions, widths, spacing, type\n  scale, tokens, component shapes), content differs, accessibility\n  corrections may deviate and are noted. Parity precedes review.\n- One heavy gate per chunk after that approval (rebuild, native acceptance,\n  the full fixture suite, the Codex review), accepted at 8 under D032/D034; the\n  phase review stays 9 and every chunk accepted at 8 is raised in C44.\n- v2 screens import no legacy feature view; the legacy files stay for the\n  legacy shell until C44 removes it. C33 was committed without a receipt (its\n  core stands; its two screens are superseded).\n- Chunks: C35 shell, C36 Home, C37 Inbox fix-up, C38 Harness, C39 Administration\n  (a: Runtime Security, b: other products), C40 Test Cases, C41 API Client,\n  C42 Academy (prototype chrome around the hosted embed), C43 Wizard re-port\n  over the existing state machine, C44 legacy removal on a branch and the P09\n  review. C34 is superseded. `Subject::LAST_CHUNK` is 44.\n\n## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\n\n- Fresh application implementation; the existing GPUI codebase is primarily a\n  reference point.\n- React presentation, Rust application implementation, and the new Rust SCM SDK.\n- Tauri was initially acceptable if needed and is now selected by D008.\n- cdot-framework informs the backend foundation through D008's selective reuse\n  and architecture direction; individual imports still require evaluation.\n- Plan first, architecture improvement review second, implementation and package\n  qualification after that.\n- Independent numeric review gates for testable chunks; earlier requirement:\n  scores below 9/10 require remediation and another actual review.\n\n## Interview exit and remaining evidence\n\nThe product/process frontier through Q23 is settled; D024/D025 subsequently\nsettle source terms and all four architecture candidates. Continue the requested\narchitecture work from those decisions. The prior extra blanket scope-confirmation\nrequest must not prevent already authorized design/research. G01 still requires\nconcrete interfaces/commands and independent review before implementation.\nExact identity strings, dependency pins, import compatibility, named numeric\nbudgets, and designated live environments require explicit evidence/specification\nat their declared gates. They are not secretly assumed complete or reasons to\nrepeat settled product questions. No application implementation has started.\n\n## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n\nDecided by the owner on 2026-10-31, in the owner's words: \"i really really really don't want to have an import from v1. in fact, i plan on calling this v1 since the previous was an alpha.\"\n\n- The previous desktop (`/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-desktop`) is the alpha. Nothing is imported from it: the reviewed import of alpha work (C23: the Import from v1 destination and view, the wizard's \"Used Prisma AIRS Desktop 1?\" box and the tenant step's import link, the first-run import frame) is removed from the one presentation in C44, its native checks C23-N01..N09 are retired without replacement, and the legacy-script map and the C44 cumulative set drop `acceptance_c23.py`.\n- Still to decide the same way, in a follow-up chunk the owner names (proposed C45): the core's alpha-import intents and reader (`import_v1_domain`, the `V1Import*` intents, the host adapters), Settings' file-based \"Import tenant profiles\" and the API Client's \"Import v1 API Client profile\" adoption, which are alpha-import surfaces too; their removal changes contracts and earlier chunks' tests and is not done inside the P09 closure.\n- Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\n- The product name shown today stays \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\" until that chunk.\n\n# C43 — Wizard re-port\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C42.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\nR2Onboard, every `step`, `filled`, `verify`, `mode=add`. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nthe presentation re-ported over the existing state machine and intents: 320px rail (244px in add mode) with brand tile, numbered steps, done checks, Optional/Skipped tags, privacy note and theme button; a pinned footer (Cancel in add mode, Back, hint, Step n of m, Skip, primary); section cards (18/20), a 2-column field grid, segmented control, switch; each step's layout per the board; the add sheet at a fixed 1160×780 without the modal's padding. Model-driven extras (credential save/remove forms, workspace chooser, unavailable products) housed inside the prototype's cards.\n\n## Core it reads\n\n`ShellSnapshot.setup`; the setup intents of C29 unchanged. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C43/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C43-N01 every step first-run; C43-N02 the add sheet; C43-N03 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_wizard` (C29's `ui_v2_onboarding` stays registered); Vitest `v2/wizard/*.test.tsx`.\n{\n  \"request_id\": \"C29-attempt-07-1793542279\",\n  \"attempt_id\": \"attempt-07\",\n  \"subject\": \"C29\",\n  \"fingerprints\": {\n    \"source\": \"d636049e5ae2d4a797cbce75a6d206c1bc18279e919b924159e2cb3f5e9cb0f1\",\n    \"dependencies\": \"e71a3a619ddb8f132ca63c6a04f63fae3d4b675ef495197c674972e52fb6cec7\",\n    \"build_flags\": \"166488b352224eb230ddfca178064d76f43deecbb6c73fb6d9359f56632e1a1f\",\n    \"evidence\": \"78aa536bc6ecdba768044cd56fd4eef26de54af04bd1783ee1843f9b0cebe029\"\n  },\n  \"scores\": {\n    \"architecture\": 9,\n    \"behavior\": 9,\n    \"authority_security\": 9,\n    \"validation\": 8,\n    \"overall\": 8\n  },\n  \"required_fixes\": [\n    \"R1 — tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py:322–325 and acceptance_c43.py:280–396: the map marks C29-N02/N03/N05 exercised by narrower C43 smoke checks. The replacement driver does not perform the Gateway workspace/key setup, rejected-client replacement and stale-verification sequence, or cancellation of a keyed draft with Keychain-removal verification. Its cancellation test creates an unkeyed draft and checks that the sheet closes. This loses mandatory native coverage while reporting the original assertions covered. Restore these assertions in the replacement driver and retain passing, source-bound native observations showing the expected verification transitions, unchanged active tenant/list after Cancel, and deletion of the cancelled draft's synthetic credential. Correct the mapping to reflect the assertions actually executed.\",\n    \"R2 — tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py:326 and acceptance_c43.py:411–477,537: C29-N06 requires every wizard step and the add sheet in both themes at 100%/200%, with keyboard traversal on each step. C43-N03 instead requires exactly eight layout rows covering only add-mode Tenant and Verify, plus one Tenant keyboard walk. The retained first-run composites cover both themes at ordinary zoom but do not close the missing 200% and keyboard coverage. Extend and execute the replacement matrix for all required steps/modes; acceptance requires hash-bound captures, AX trees and traversal results for the complete matrix.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [\n    \"E1 — docs/planning/evidence/C44/native/cumulative/C43/native-acceptance.json does not establish the retained native behavior assertions identified in R1. The historical C29 record covers the earlier presentation; it does not supply native acceptance of those interactions after the C43 re-port. These assertions are marked exercised, not retired.\",\n    \"E2 — Current-presentation evidence for the complete C29-N06/T09 matrix is missing. The mapped C43-N03 record explicitly limits its layouts to add-mode Tenant and Verify. Passing component tests and historical screenshots cannot substitute for the required native matrix.\"\n  ],\n  \"optional_suggestions\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Reproduced all four supplied fingerprints. All 444 scoped file hashes and 18,337 compiled-input inventory entries matched, including the final recheck. Before/after inventories were identical; all 18 listed run-log hashes matched. These checks establish consistency under the supplied hashing procedures, not compiler or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Verified C28's receipt hash and matching passing raw verdict; also checked C27's passing verdict against its receipt. D058 authorizes proceeding while C26 remains open; controller completion and the P09 phase gate remain separate.\",\n    \"Independently ran the retained onboarding binary: 10/10 passed; the retained IPC setup secret-confinement test: 1/1 passed; and the two offline L19 settlement regressions: 2/2 passed. The Rust binaries were not rebuilt or independently authenticated against compiler inputs. Broader results rely on retained logs, including 541 desktop tests and the recorded core, host, controller and build checks.\",\n    \"The L19 receipt and retained AX tree support successful management verification, with the placeholder scan key reported Stored. Verified the live receipt/build hash chain and current qualification executable hash. Recomputed the qualification-to-current source differences: the ten disclosed Harness/tooling files differ; scoped wizard/core/host/contracts inputs match. No live operation was independently repeated, and HTTP request counts were not observed.\",\n    \"The mapped C43 record matches its originating C44 preparation hash. All 52 scoped application/core/contracts files checked against C44's compiled-input inventory matched. The historical C44 executable has been replaced at its bundle path; the current executable matches P09's preparation, not the older C43 acceptance. Native conclusions therefore rely on retained records, AX trees and captures.\",\n    \"Inspected the retained wizard AX trees and three representative captures. Did not drive native UI, record spoken VoiceOver, exercise hosted Academy sign-in, inspect private authorization manifests or access credentials. Repository-recorded owner authorization was not independently authenticated.\",\n    \"No application files were changed, product endpoints called or OS permissions granted. The sandbox is read-only; this returned JSON must be persisted as the verdict artifact.\"\n  ],\n  \"inspected_files\": [\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\n    \"GLOSSARY.md\",\n    \"docs/adr/0001-native-operation-authority.md\",\n    \"docs/adr/0002-academy-shared-presentation.md\",\n    \"docs/adr/0003-native-harness-and-scoped-identity.md\",\n    \"docs/adr/0004-managed-workbench-admission.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/decisions.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/status.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/dependencies.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/parity-matrix.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/test-catalogue.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/review-protocol.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/live-checks.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/chunks/C29.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/chunks/C43.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/chunks/C44.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/review-verdict.schema.json\",\n    \"docs/architecture/checks.json\",\n    \"docs/architecture/native-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/state-ownership.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/wizard.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C29/attempt-07/request.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C29/attempt-07/source-inventory.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C29/attempt-06/verdict-returned.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C29/remediation-attempt-05.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C27/attempt-05/receipt.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C27/attempt-05/verdict.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C28/attempt-09/receipt.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C28/attempt-09/verdict.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C44/attempt-05/request.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C44/attempt-05/source-inventory.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C44/attempt-05/receipt.json\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/C44/legacy-retirements.md\",\n    \"apps/desktop/academy-source.ts\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/app.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/modal.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/wizard/wizard.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/wizard/copy.ts\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/wizard/wizard.test.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/v2/wizard/wizard-boards.test.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src/features/academy/academy-account.tsx\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/keychain.rs\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/tests/ipc_admission.rs\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/main.json\",\n    \"apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/setup_domain.rs\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/management_domain.rs\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/gateway_domain.rs\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs\",\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs\",\n    \"crat