{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'fn tree_hash|fn file_entry|fn inventory_hash|fn hash_inventory|update\\\\(' crates/xtask/src/fingerprint.rs; sed -n '1,185p' crates/xtask/src/fingerprint.rs; cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/shell.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/academy.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/inbox-reads.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/api-client-test-cases.md\"","aggregated_output":"94:fn file_entry(root: &Path, relative: &str) -> Result<FileEntry> {\n120:pub fn inventory_hash(entries: &[FileEntry]) -> String {\n133:pub fn tree_hash(dir: &Path) -> Result<String> {\n138:pub fn tree_hash_excluding(dir: &Path, skip: &[&str]) -> Result<String> {\n//! Input fingerprints bound into review packets and receipts.\n//!\n//! * source: every tracked or untracked-but-not-ignored file (path, mode,\n//!   content or symlink target) plus the repository `.git/config`, minus a\n//!   narrow set of mutable evidence locations that are hashed separately.\n//! * dependencies: lockfiles, toolchain pin, the consumed immutable inputs\n//!   under `.inputs/`, and the resolved build-tool identities.\n//! * build_flags: the subject's manifest entries, Tauri configuration and\n//!   capability files, target and fixture-feature policy.\n//! * evidence: the subject's committed evidence directory.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse crate::manifest::Manifest;\nuse crate::{Repo, Result, Subject, invalid, io_err, sha256_hex};\n\n/// Mutable locations excluded from the source fingerprint. Each is hashed\n/// independently (evidence fingerprint, receipts) so exclusion cannot hide\n/// application sources, lockfiles, tests or configuration.\npub const SOURCE_EXCLUSIONS: [&str; 3] = [\n    \"docs/planning/status.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/\",\n    \"docs/planning/evidence/\",\n];\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct Fingerprints {\n    pub source: String,\n    pub dependencies: String,\n    pub build_flags: String,\n    pub evidence: String,\n}\n\n/// One entry of the source inventory.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct FileEntry {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub mode: String,\n    pub sha256: String,\n}\n\npub fn is_excluded(path: &str) -> bool {\n    SOURCE_EXCLUSIONS.iter().any(|excluded| {\n        if excluded.ends_with('/') {\n            path.starts_with(excluded)\n        } else {\n            path == *excluded\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n/// Lists source files via git: tracked plus untracked files not ignored.\npub fn source_inventory(repo: &Repo) -> Result<Vec<FileEntry>> {\n    let output = Command::new(\"/usr/bin/git\")\n        .args([\n            \"ls-files\",\n            \"-z\",\n            \"--cached\",\n            \"--others\",\n            \"--exclude-standard\",\n        ])\n        .current_dir(repo.root())\n        .env_clear()\n        .env(\"PATH\", \"/usr/bin:/bin\")\n        .env(\"HOME\", std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_default())\n        .output()\n        .map_err(io_err(repo.root()))?;\n    if !output.status.success() {\n        return Err(invalid(\"git ls-files failed\"));\n    }\n    let mut paths: Vec<String> = output\n        .stdout\n        .split(|b| *b == 0)\n        .filter(|p| !p.is_empty())\n        .map(|p| String::from_utf8_lossy(p).into_owned())\n        .filter(|p| !is_excluded(p))\n        .collect();\n    paths.sort();\n    paths.dedup();\n    let mut entries = Vec::with_capacity(paths.len() + 1);\n    for path in paths {\n        entries.push(file_entry(repo.root(), &path)?);\n    }\n    entries.push(file_entry(repo.root(), \".git/config\")?);\n    Ok(entries)\n}\n\nfn file_entry(root: &Path, relative: &str) -> Result<FileEntry> {\n    let full = root.join(relative);\n    let Ok(meta) = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&full) else {\n        return Ok(FileEntry {\n            path: relative.to_owned(),\n            mode: \"deleted\".to_owned(),\n            sha256: String::new(),\n        });\n    };\n    if meta.file_type().is_symlink() {\n        let target = std::fs::read_link(&full).map_err(io_err(&full))?;\n        return Ok(FileEntry {\n            path: relative.to_owned(),\n            mode: \"symlink\".to_owned(),\n            sha256: sha256_hex(target.as_os_str().as_encoded_bytes()),\n        });\n    }\n    let bytes = std::fs::read(&full).map_err(io_err(&full))?;\n    let executable = meta.permissions().mode() & 0o111 != 0;\n    Ok(FileEntry {\n        path: relative.to_owned(),\n        mode: if executable { \"100755\" } else { \"100644\" }.to_owned(),\n        sha256: sha256_hex(&bytes),\n    })\n}\n\npub fn inventory_hash(entries: &[FileEntry]) -> String {\n    let text: String = entries\n        .iter()\n        .map(|e| format!(\"{}\\0{}\\0{}\\n\", e.path, e.mode, e.sha256))\n        .collect();\n    sha256_hex(text.as_bytes())\n}\n\npub fn source(repo: &Repo) -> Result<String> {\n    Ok(inventory_hash(&source_inventory(repo)?))\n}\n\n/// Hash of every regular file under a directory (relative paths, sorted).\npub fn tree_hash(dir: &Path) -> Result<String> {\n    tree_hash_excluding(dir, &[])\n}\n\n/// Like [`tree_hash`], skipping directories with the given names.\npub fn tree_hash_excluding(dir: &Path, skip: &[&str]) -> Result<String> {\n    let mut entries = Vec::new();\n    collect_tree(dir, dir, skip, &mut entries)?;\n    entries.sort_by(|a, b| a.path.cmp(&b.path));\n    Ok(inventory_hash(&entries))\n}\n\nfn collect_tree(root: &Path, dir: &Path, skip: &[&str], out: &mut Vec<FileEntry>) -> Result<()> {\n    let mut children: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(dir)\n        .map_err(io_err(dir))?\n        .filter_map(|e| e.ok())\n        .collect();\n    children.sort_by_key(|e| e.file_name());\n    for child in children {\n        let path = child.path();\n        let relative = path\n            .strip_prefix(root)\n            .map_err(|_| invalid(\"path escaped its root\"))?\n            .to_string_lossy()\n            .into_owned();\n        let meta = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&path).map_err(io_err(&path))?;\n        if meta.is_dir() {\n            if skip.iter().any(|name| child.file_name() == *name) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            collect_tree(root, &path, skip, out)?;\n        } else {\n            out.push(file_entry(root, &relative)?);\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// Dependency inputs: lockfiles, toolchain pin, immutable inputs, tools.\npub fn dependencies(repo: &Repo, toolchain_hash: &str) -> Result<String> {\n    let mut parts: BTreeMap<String, String> = BTreeMap::new();\n    for file in [\n        \"Cargo.lock\",\n        \"pnpm-lock.yaml\",\n        \"rust-toolchain.toml\",\n        \".npmrc\",\n        \"docs/architecture/inputs.lock.json\",\n    ] {\n        let path = repo.join(file);\n        let digest = match std::fs::read(&path) {\n            Ok(bytes) => sha256_hex(&bytes),\n            Err(_) => \"absent\".to_owned(),\n        };\n# Shell, Home, tenant switcher, palette, toasts\n\nSource: `prototype/R2App.dc.html` (sidebar markup, `nav`, `switchPatch`,\n`requestSwitch`, `palette*`, `toast*`, `top`, Home section). Chunk: C28 (shell,\nHome skeleton), C30 (Home attention list backed by Inbox scope).\n\n## Sidebar\n\n- Top: tenant switcher button showing tenant name and environment pill;\n  ⌘T opens the list. Entries: every tenant (name, environment, TSG), then\n  \"Add a tenant…\". Selected tenant uses `sel/selInk`.\n- Destinations in the order of DESIGN-V2 §5 with icon, label, shortcut hint.\n  Unavailable destinations render disabled with their availability reason as\n  a tooltip and accessible description, never hidden.\n- Bottom: appearance toggle (light/dark/system) and \"Show the calls\" toggle,\n  both dispatching their Rust preference.\n- Collapses to icons below 1280px window width.\n\n## Home\n\n- Title \"Home\" with the tenant name and environment beneath; last-read line\n  from `ReadStatus` (\"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  \"· 3 sources partial\", warn-styled when partial; \"First read pending\" on a\n  fresh tenant).\n- \"Needs attention\": up to five Inbox items of kind Needs action, each with\n  severity (colour + icon + word), title, product, action button that\n  navigates with context, Acknowledge, and Snooze whose tooltip and\n  accessible name are the item's `snoozeLabel`.\n- Product cards for admitted, licensed products with their read state;\n  unlicensed products are listed once as \"Not licensed in this tenant\" and\n  unavailable products once as \"Not available in this release\" (DESIGN-V2\n  §6), never hidden.\n- Playground card (Runtime Security scan): prompt, direction, profile select,\n  verdict panel (word + icon + reason + plain explanation). Verdicts are\n  profile-aware: a detector not enabled, or a topic not assigned, reads \"Not\n  detected\" with the reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged with the\n  profile named.\n\n## Tenant switch (I1, I2)\n\n- `switchTenant{tenant_id, resolution?}`; the core refuses with\n  `SwitchBlocked{pending: {conversation, decision}}` when a Harness decision is\n  pending. The UI renders the guard dialog (Archive and switch / Discard and\n  switch / Stay) from that payload and re-dispatches with `resolution`. Initial\n  focus is on Stay, the safe default (Enter on arrival never ends the\n  conversation); Archive and switch stays the visually primary action.\n- Every entry point (switcher, palette, menu, wizard completion) uses the same\n  intent. After a switch the new tenant's Home renders from cached scopes within\n  100 ms with read status pending until the read lands.\n\n## Command palette\n\n- ⌘K. Entries: destinations from the Rust inventory, tenants, and three actions\n  (Navigate, Switch tenant, Read now). Typing filters; Enter dispatches; Escape\n  closes and restores focus. Native menu navigation while the palette is open\n  closes it first.\n\n## Toasts (I10)\n\n- Kinds ok, info, warn with icon and colour; one visible at a time, newest\n  replaces; 6 s expiry (persist under Reduce Motion); optional Undo action\n  (snooze). A toast never carries information absent from an observed scope.\n\n## Modals (I8)\n\n- Stack order kept in the shell store; only the topmost is interactive;\n  siblings get `aria-hidden`; Escape closes the topmost; focus returns to the\n  opener. Detail sheets (transcripts, facts) are modals in this stack.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Fixture boards: R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2App default.\n- V2-T01, T02, T09, T10, T11; V2-N01, N03, N04, N05.\n# Academy embed\n\nSource: `R2App` Academy section, board R2Academy. Chunk: C34.\n\nThe Academy learner view (react-query, react-router, Academy ShellFrame) is\nhosted inside the new shell unchanged: the new sidebar replaces its outer\nframe, its inner routing and tests stay intact. Gamification appears only\nhere. The wizard's Academy step is the only other Academy surface.\n\nTokens: Academy's `--academy-*` variables remain its own; within the embed\nscope the shell aliases nothing. The embed receives the Rust-owned theme.\n\nTests: existing Academy presentation tests unchanged; one shell test that the\nembed mounts under `academy` and receives theme changes.\n# Inbox and reads\n\nSource: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,\n`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.\n\n## Inbox\n\n- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity\n  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line (\"API keys · cached\",\n  \"rotated 07:46\"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:\n  body, facts table, \"Why this matters\" explanation, action button (navigates\n  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.\n- Empty states distinguish \"first read pending\" from \"nothing needs action\"\n  and name partial sources (\"3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45\").\n- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in\n  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no\n  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and\n  Snoozed-tab \"Returns …\" text all state the same time (I11). The\n  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.\n- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,\n  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint\n  offering \"Open the saved transcript\" and \"Start a new investigation\".\n\n## Reads (I4)\n\n- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`\n  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read\n  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.\n- Completion toast: ok \"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  warn \"· 3 sources partial\"; for fresh tenants \"· 1 product still needs a\n  role\" or \"· no activity yet in <tenant>\". `recheckProduct` after a role is\n  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.\n\n## Core contract\n\n- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,\n  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`\n  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,\n  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.\n- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from\n  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back\n  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.\n# API Client and Test Cases\n\nSource: `R2App` (`REQ`, `hist`, `send`, `rawJson`, `CASES`, `packCases`,\n`caseRows` lines 1033–1037, `runScan`). Chunk: C33. Both are re-skins of the\nexisting workbench (C14–C15) and library (C12) modules to the layout rhythm.\nNo new remote capability is introduced.\n\n## API Client\n\n- Title row, request tabs (named requests per product), method/URL line with\n  the `get` colour, Send (32px), response pane with status, duration and\n  body; history list of immutable snapshots (I5) from the existing workbench\n  history.\n- After Send, a compact `role=\"status\"` region announces \"<request> · <code>\n  · <duration>\"; the JSON body is outside the live region.\n- Generic requests never bypass AIRS mutation authority (existing C15 rule):\n  a request that would change configuration is refused by the core as today.\n- The \"Show the calls\" panel reuses this response renderer.\n\n## Test Cases\n\n- Title row, filter by product, search, paged table (name, product, input,\n  last result as verdict colour + icon + word), pack-sourced cases carry\n  their pack name.\n- **Runtime-only execution boundary** (prototype lines 1035–1037, parity\n  matrix). A Runtime Security case offers \"Open in Playground\": it sets the\n  Playground's prompt, direction and profile and the operator runs the scan\n  there; the result is stored for the case as a local Playground run. A case\n  for any other product offers \"Inspect\" only: it opens the specification\n  and the recorded result, states which product runs it, and never\n  dispatches a scan or claims execution. Red Team cases say \"hand the spec\n  to a scan\"; no scan is started from this screen.\n- Starter-pack cases selected in the wizard are written at onboarding\n  completion as library entries with `Not run` results.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Boards R2Api, R2Cases. Tests V2-R05, V2-T05; V2-T14 status region updates\n  after Send with the body outside the live region; V2-T15 non-Runtime rows\n  render Inspect, never Open in Playground, and clicking Inspect dispatches\n  no scan intent (asserted on the mock runtime); V2-T16 paging and filter.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
